  :adr/body
  "# ADR-2607184100: Opt-in native transport provider for Kotoba components

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-18
**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki

## Context

ADR-2607184000 fixed the bounded socket/TLS ABI and implemented compiler
validation, Kotoba HTTP/DB provider sources, and a fail-closed kototama binding
seam. It deliberately left the native binding unavailable.

## Decision

Implement an explicit JVM/Chicory transport provider. It is never installed
implicitly: a caller constructs it from normalized HostCaps and injects its
HostFunctions into `kototama.tender/open-session`.

The provider keeps Java Socket and SSLSocket objects in a private handle table.
Wasm sees only nonzero affine i64 handles. Connect requires an exact lowercase
`host:port` member of `:transport-endpoint-allowlist`, a finite connection
count, and a finite connect timeout. Read and write enforce cumulative byte
limits. Close consumes the handle. TLS consumes the underlying TCP handle,
requires the server name to equal the scoped host, enables HTTPS endpoint
identification and SNI, and performs the handshake before returning a new
handle. Failures return zero or minus one and never expose descriptors or Java
objects.

## Maturity boundary

This establishes real local TCP execution through the Wasm ABI and implements
the TLS binding. It remains an opt-in JVM compatibility prototype. Browser and
Node providers, certificate-policy customization, broad protocol conformance,
component-to-component linking, production CI/soak, and Q9 consumer cutover
remain pending.
"}]
